.TH OROC-SETUP 1 "" "Oro Runtime 0.1.4" "Oro Runtime Manual"
.SH NAME
oroc\-setup \- Setup build tools for host or target platform.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
oroc setup [options] [\-\-platform=<platform>] [\-y|\-\-yes]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Setup build tools for host or target platform.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-platform=<platform>\fR
platform target to run setup for (defaults to host):
.br
\(bu android
.br
\(bu ios
.br
\(bu linux
.br
\(bu windows
.TP
\fB\-q, \-\-quiet\fR
hint for less log output
.TP
\fB\-y, \-\-yes\fR
answer yes to any prompts
.SH COMMON ERRORS
.PP
Without `\-\-platform`, setup defaults to the host. Verify with `oroc env`.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBoroc setup \-\-platform=android\fR
install or validate Android SDK/NDK requirements
.TP
\fBoroc setup \-\-platform=ios\fR
install or validate host tools needed for iOS/macOS builds
.SH SEE ALSO
oroc(1)
